  name: Global ship traffic
  notebooks:
    - blocks:
        - id: e5a7d14addbd4dd597e012dfb2124278
          blockGroup: 2d859668355049aba17570e2b93515bd
          sortingKey: "000000"
          type: markdown
          content: >-
            # Ships Global — data build


            Builds the data for this project's app (`_deepnote_static/index.html`): a 3D globe / flat map of six years
            of global ship traffic.


            **Source:** World Bank / IMF [Global Shipping Traffic
            Density](https://datacatalog.worldbank.org/search/dataset/0037580) (CC BY 4.0). It is a 0.005° grid of AIS
            position reports for Jan 2015 – Feb 2021, all vessel types. Land comes from Natural Earth 1:10m.


            **Run all** (about 20 min; the download only happens on the first run):

            1. Download the 535 MB zip and extract the 9.8 GB GeoTIFF to local disk.

            2. Inspect the raster.

            3. Process it into `_deepnote_static/data/`:
               - 648 tiles of 10° at 0.01°;
               - an 8192 × 4096 global texture;
               - 320k sparkle points;
               - `meta.json` with concentration, passage shares and the longitude profile.
            4. Put three.js in the app folder.


            The raw values sum AIS reports, not vessel-hours, so the app shows only relative measures: shares, multiples
            of the ocean average, and percentiles.
          metadata: {}
        - id: e3d4d1ef7fee4ed38da33916f9914de9
          blockGroup: 20af1c3006d743dcb912cde358da7bf0
          sortingKey: "000001"
          outputs: []
          type: code
          content: >-
            # 1 · Download the World Bank / IMF Global Shipping Traffic Density raster (~535 MB, once)

            #     The zip stays in project storage; the 9.8 GB GeoTIFF is extracted to the machine's local disk for fast
            reads.

            import os, subprocess, sys, zipfile, time, shutil

            from pathlib import Path

            subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-m", "pip", "install", "-q", "rasterio", "shapely>=2", "pillow"],
            check=True)


            RAW = Path("data/raw"); RAW.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

            URL = "https://datacatalogfiles.worldbank.org/ddh-published/0037580/DR0045406/shipdensity_global.zip"

            ZIP = RAW / "shipdensity_global.zip"

            if not ZIP.exists() or ZIP.stat().st_size < 534_000_000:
                t = time.time()
                subprocess.run(["curl", "-sSfL", "-A", "Mozilla/5.0", "-o", str(ZIP), URL], check=True)
                print(f"downloaded {ZIP.stat().st_size/1e6:.0f} MB in {time.time()-t:.0f} s")

            TMP = Path("/tmp/shipdensity"); TMP.mkdir(exist_ok=True)

            TIF = TMP / "shipdensity_global.tif"

            if not TIF.exists() or TIF.stat().st_size < 9_800_000_000:
                t = time.time()
                with zipfile.ZipFile(ZIP) as z:
                    for n in ["shipdensity_global.tif", "shipdensity_global.tfw", "shipdensity_global.tif.aux.xml"]: z.extract(n, TMP)
                print(f"extracted in {time.time()-t:.0f} s")
            for f in ["shipdensity_global.tif", "shipdensity_global.tif.ovr"]:  # an earlier run extracted into project
            storage; not needed there
                if (RAW / f).exists(): (RAW / f).unlink()
            print("geotransform (.tfw):", (TMP / "shipdensity_global.tfw").read_text().split())

            print(shutil.disk_usage("/tmp"))
          metadata: {}
        - id: 73d0116e5af141fc9704b61ae07c6afb
          blockGroup: 227f9174b38048d899c3371d6ea860a9
          sortingKey: "000002"
          outputs: []
          type: code
          content: >-
            # 2 · Inspect: 72 006 × 33 998 int32 cells of 0.005°, from 180.0128°W / 85.0001°N.

            #     Value = number of hourly AIS positions in the cell, Jan 2015 – Feb 2021 (IMF World Seaborne Trade
            Monitoring System).

            import rasterio

            with rasterio.open(TIF) as src:
                print(src.width, src.height, src.dtypes, src.nodata, src.transform, src.crs, sep="\n")
          metadata: {}
        - id: e0d641f0af274b00a02b4bcfb1233769
          blockGroup: da0f791530e5430986c4c7f908d647f8
          sortingKey: "000003"
          outputs: []
          type: code
          content: >-
            # 3 · Process for the app (writes _deepnote_static/data/…)

            #   tiles/{ty}_{tx}.png  10°×10° tiles at 0.01° (1000×1000 px), loaded when the viewer zooms in

            #   global.png           8192×4096 equirectangular texture of the whole world (0.044°)

            #   Each PNG: R = log(1 + density) in 8 bits, G = anti-aliased land cover (Natural Earth 1:10m), B = 0

            #   particles.bin        sparkle points sampled by density;  meta.json  passages, concentration, profiles

            #

            # Units: the raster sums AIS position reports per cell over Jan 2015 – Feb 2021. The global total (~6.6e14)
            is far more than

            # one report per ship per hour, so absolute values are not vessel-hours. Everything shown in the app is
            therefore relative:

            # shares of the world total, multiples of the ocean average, and percentiles.

            import json, math, requests, numpy as np

            from rasterio.windows import Window

            from PIL import Image, ImageDraw

            from shapely.geometry import shape, box

            from shapely.strtree import STRtree

            Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = None


            OUT = Path("_deepnote_static/data"); (OUT / "tiles").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

            NODATA, LOGMAX = 2147483647, math.log1p(65468393)   # HistMax from the .aux.xml = densest 0.005° cell

            COL0 = 3                                         # raster starts at 180.0128°W; dropping 3 columns aligns it
            to 180°W (±0.002°)

            OCEAN_KM2, KM_DEG = 361.1e6, 111.32


            # --- land polygons (Natural Earth 1:10m land + minor islands)

            geoms = []

            for k in ["land", "minor_islands"]:
                f = RAW / f"ne_10m_{k}.geojson"
                if not f.exists():
                    f.write_bytes(requests.get(f"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector/master/geojson/ne_10m_{k}.geojson", timeout=300).content)
                for ft in json.loads(f.read_text())["features"]:
                    g = shape(ft["geometry"]); geoms += list(g.geoms) if g.geom_type == "MultiPolygon" else [g]
            geoms = [g.buffer(0) for g in geoms]

            tree = STRtree(geoms)


            def land(lon0, lat1, wdeg, hdeg, W, H, ss=3):
                """Anti-aliased land cover 0..255 for the box whose top-left corner is (lon0, lat1)."""
                im = Image.new("L", (W * ss, H * ss), 0); d = ImageDraw.Draw(im)
                sx, sy = W * ss / wdeg, H * ss / hdeg
                pts = lambda ring: [((x - lon0) * sx, (lat1 - y) * sy) for x, y in ring.coords]
                bx = box(lon0 - 0.01, lat1 - hdeg - 0.01, lon0 + wdeg + 0.01, lat1 + 0.01)
                for i in tree.query(bx):
                    g = geoms[i] if wdeg >= 360 else geoms[i].intersection(bx)   # clip big continents to the tile
                    for p in ([g] if g.geom_type == "Polygon" else [q for q in getattr(g, "geoms", []) if q.geom_type == "Polygon"]):
                        if p.is_empty: continue
                        d.polygon(pts(p.exterior), fill=255)
                        for r in p.interiors: d.polygon(pts(r), fill=0)
                return np.asarray(im.resize((W, H), Image.BOX))

            def encode(mean_counts, landcover):
                e = np.round(np.log1p(mean_counts) / LOGMAX * 255).clip(0, 255).astype(np.uint8)
                return Image.fromarray(np.dstack([e, landcover, np.zeros_like(e)]), "RGB")

            # Passages: a 100 km × 100 km box centred on each one, so the shares are comparable

            PASSAGES = {
                "Dover Strait": (1.45, 51.0), "Singapore Strait": (103.85, 1.2), "Strait of Malacca": (101.2, 2.6),
                "Strait of Hormuz": (56.4, 26.4), "Strait of Gibraltar": (-5.6, 35.95), "Bab el-Mandeb": (43.35, 12.6),
                "Suez Canal": (32.35, 30.6), "Panama Canal": (-79.7, 9.15), "Bosphorus": (29.05, 41.1),
                "Taiwan Strait": (119.8, 24.2), "Korea Strait": (129.3, 34.6), "Øresund": (12.7, 55.9),
                "Cape of Good Hope": (18.4, -34.9), "Mona Passage": (-67.9, 18.2),
            }

            HALF_KM = 50

            REGIONS = {k: (lo - HALF_KM / (KM_DEG * math.cos(math.radians(la))), la - HALF_KM / KM_DEG,
                           lo + HALF_KM / (KM_DEG * math.cos(math.radians(la))), la + HALF_KM / KM_DEG) for k, (lo, la) in PASSAGES.items()}
            reg = {k: 0.0 for k in REGIONS}

            G = np.zeros((4500, 9000), np.float32)   # 0.04° global grid (mean value per 0.005° cell), 90°N → 90°S

            total, t0 = 0.0, time.time()

            with rasterio.open(TIF) as src:
                for b, lat_top in enumerate(range(90, -90, -10)):
                    r0 = round((85.0001479370 - lat_top) / 0.005)
                    band = np.zeros((2000, 72000), np.float32)
                    a, z = max(r0, 0), min(r0 + 2000, src.height)
                    for s in range(a, z, 500):  # read in 500-row slabs to cap memory
                        arr = src.read(1, window=Window(COL0, s, 72000, min(500, z - s)))
                        arr[(arr == NODATA) | (arr < 0)] = 0
                        band[s - r0:s - r0 + arr.shape[0]] = arr
                    total += float(band.sum(dtype=np.float64))
                    for k, (x0, y0, x1, y1) in REGIONS.items():
                        if y1 <= lat_top - 10 or y0 >= lat_top: continue
                        ra, rz = max(0, round((lat_top - y1) / .005)), min(2000, round((lat_top - y0) / .005))
                        ca, cz = round((x0 + 180) / .005), round((x1 + 180) / .005)
                        reg[k] += float(band[ra:rz, ca:cz].sum(dtype=np.float64))
                    G[b * 250:(b + 1) * 250] = band.reshape(250, 8, 9000, 8).mean(axis=(1, 3))
                    T = band.reshape(1000, 2, 36000, 2).mean(axis=(1, 3)); del band
                    for tx in range(36):
                        encode(T[:, tx * 1000:(tx + 1) * 1000], land(-180 + 10 * tx, lat_top, 10, 10, 1000, 1000)).save(OUT / f"tiles/{b}_{tx}.png", optimize=True)
                    print(f"band {lat_top:>3}° done · {time.time() - t0:.0f} s", flush=True)

            # --- global texture 8192×4096

            g8 = np.asarray(Image.fromarray(G, "F").resize((8192, 4096), Image.BOX))

            encode(g8, land(-180, 90, 360, 180, 8192, 4096, ss=2)).save(OUT / "global.png", optimize=True)


            # --- concentration: the smallest share of the ocean that holds 50% / 90% / 99% of all traffic

            lat_c = 90 - (np.arange(4500) + .5) * .04

            cell_km2 = (0.04 * KM_DEG) ** 2 * np.cos(np.radians(lat_c))[:, None] * np.ones((1, 9000), np.float32)

            vol = (G * 64).ravel().astype(np.float64)                     # sum of the 64 source cells

            dens = vol / cell_km2.ravel()

            o = np.argsort(-dens); cv = np.cumsum(vol[o]) / vol.sum(); ca = np.cumsum(cell_km2.ravel()[o])

            conc = {str(q): float(ca[np.searchsorted(cv, q / 100)] / OCEAN_KM2 * 100) for q in (50, 90, 99)}


            # --- sparkle particles: 320k points, probability ∝ density^0.55, jittered inside their 0.04° cell

            rng = np.random.default_rng(7)

            w = np.power(G.ravel().astype(np.float64), 0.55); w /= w.sum()

            idx = rng.choice(w.size, 320_000, p=w)

            iy, ix = np.divmod(idx, 9000)

            lon = -180 + (ix + rng.random(idx.size)) * 0.04; lat = 90 - (iy + rng.random(idx.size)) * 0.04

            lv = np.log1p(G.ravel()[idx]) / LOGMAX

            order = np.argsort(rng.random(idx.size))

            with open(OUT / "particles.bin", "wb") as f:
                f.write(np.round((lon[order] + 180) / 360 * 65535).astype("<u2").tobytes())
                f.write(np.round((lat[order] + 90) / 180 * 65535).astype("<u2").tobytes())
                f.write(np.round(lv[order] * 255).astype("u1").tobytes())

            g1 = G.reshape(180, 25, 360, 25).sum(axis=(1, 3)) * 64

            meta = {
                "source": "World Bank / IMF Global Shipping Traffic Density (CC BY 4.0), built from IMF AIS position reports",
                "period": "Jan 2015 – Feb 2021", "logmax": LOGMAX, "total": total,
                "mean_per_cell": total / (OCEAN_KM2 / (0.005 * KM_DEG) ** 2),   # ocean-average value of an equatorial 0.005° cell
                "concentration": conc,
                "tiles": {"deg": 10, "px": 1000, "rows": 18, "cols": 36},
                "passage_km": 2 * HALF_KM,
                "regions": [{"name": k, "center": PASSAGES[k], "box": [round(v, 4) for v in REGIONS[k]], "share": v / total}
                            for k, v in sorted(reg.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1])],
                "lon_profile": (g1.sum(axis=0) / total).round(6).tolist(), "lat_profile": (g1.sum(axis=1) / total).round(6).tolist(),
                "built_at": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()),
            }

            (OUT / "meta.json").write_text(json.dumps(meta))

            sizes = sum(p.stat().st_size for p in OUT.rglob("*") if p.is_file())

            print(f"half of all traffic uses {conc['50']:.2f}% of the ocean, 90% uses {conc['90']:.1f}%, 99% uses
            {conc['99']:.1f}%")

            print(f"output {sizes / 1e6:.0f} MB · global.png {(OUT / 'global.png').stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB ·
            {time.time() - t0:.0f} s")

            for r in meta["regions"]: print(f"  {r['name']:<22} {r['share'] * 100:6.3f}% of world traffic")
          metadata: {}
        - id: 3810329928924de5aaf036070e562c51
          blockGroup: 9fa507a76987438ab601ec07b06342cd
          sortingKey: "000004"
          outputs: []
          type: code
          content: >-
            # 4 · App runtime: three.js served from the app folder (no CDN needed); the app itself is
            _deepnote_static/index.html

            V = Path("_deepnote_static/vendor"); V.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

            if not (V / "three.min.js").exists():
                (V / "three.min.js").write_bytes(requests.get("https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.149.0/build/three.min.js", timeout=120).content)
            print("three.js", (V / "three.min.js").stat().st_size // 1024, "KB ·", len(list((OUT /
            "tiles").glob("*.png"))), "tiles")
          metadata: {}
      executionMode: block
      id: 2fe30e69dd3744499c586ed198d8cbd2
      isModule: false
      name: Build data
  settings: {}
